From: DevOps Hero <doh@devopshero.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] Stash Bedrock TTFT timestamps on the agent instance

Pinned upstream: v2026.4.30, run_agent.py.

Purpose: give DOH's WebUI patch a way to attribute chat sluggishness to
"Bedrock" vs "our stack" without adding any new log lines. We record two
monotonic timestamps on the AIAgent instance:

  _perf_bedrock_send_at        — just before the provider streaming call
  _perf_bedrock_first_delta_at — first time _fire_first[_delta]() runs

The WebUI reads these from the agent instance in api/streaming.py on the
first on_token() and emits a one-shot `perf` SSE event for the browser to
console.log. The attributes are overwritten on every turn (single-writer
from the streaming thread), so later turns don't reuse stale values.

Claude on Bedrock and other Bedrock models take different code paths:

  - Non-Claude Bedrock (Nova, Llama, DeepSeek, Titan, etc.) use the
    boto3 `converse_stream()` call inside the `bedrock_converse` branch
    of `_interruptible_streaming_api_call`. The first two hunks stamp
    that path.

  - Claude on Bedrock uses the `AnthropicBedrock` SDK's
    `messages.stream(**api_kwargs)` path inside the `anthropic_messages`
    branch. Hunks 3 and 4 stamp that path, gated on
    `self.provider == "bedrock"` so native Anthropic / MiniMax / other
    anthropic_messages callers don't get stamped (the WebUI gate would
    suppress emission anyway, but this keeps agent state clean).

Upstream status: no open PR — DOH-specific telemetry. Revisit if upstream
adds structured per-provider TTFT metrics.

--- a/run_agent.py
+++ b/run_agent.py
@@ -6592,6 +6592,7 @@
             def _fire_first():
                 if not first_delta_fired["done"] and on_first_delta:
                     first_delta_fired["done"] = True
+                    self._perf_bedrock_first_delta_at = time.monotonic()
                     try:
                         on_first_delta()
                     except Exception:
@@ -6609,6 +6610,9 @@
                     api_kwargs.pop("__bedrock_converse__", None)
                     client = _get_bedrock_runtime_client(region)
                     try:
+                        # DOH TTFT telemetry: stamp just before the blocking
+                        # converse_stream() so WebUI can attribute latency.
+                        self._perf_bedrock_send_at = time.monotonic()
                         raw_response = client.converse_stream(**api_kwargs)
                     except Exception as _bedrock_exc:
                         # Evict the cached client on stale-connection failures
@@ -6662,6 +6666,13 @@
         def _fire_first_delta():
             if not first_delta_fired["done"] and on_first_delta:
                 first_delta_fired["done"] = True
+                # DOH TTFT telemetry: stamp on the anthropic_messages path
+                # too (Claude-on-Bedrock uses AnthropicBedrock SDK, not
+                # boto3 converse_stream). Only for bedrock provider — other
+                # anthropic_messages callers (native Anthropic, MiniMax,
+                # etc.) don't need this and the WebUI gate won't emit.
+                if getattr(self, "provider", "") == "bedrock":
+                    self._perf_bedrock_first_delta_at = time.monotonic()
                 try:
                     on_first_delta()
                 except Exception:
@@ -6932,6 +6943,11 @@

